<div class="shell">
  {%- if settings.prototype_banner != blank -%}
    <p class="prototype-banner">{{ settings.prototype_banner }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <nav class="hint" style="padding-top:1rem;" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url | default: '/' }}">Home</a>
    {%- for c in product.breadcrumbs -%} · <a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.title }}</a>{%- endfor -%}
  </nav>

  <div class="product">
    <div class="product__media">
      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
        <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 900 }}" alt="{{ product.title | escape }}" width="900" height="900">
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if product.description != blank -%}
        <section style="margin-top:1.5rem;max-width:var(--measure);">
          <h2 style="font-size:1rem;">Details</h2>
          <div class="rte">{{ product.description }}</div>
        </section>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div>
      {%- if product.vendor != blank -%}<p class="card__eyebrow">{{ product.vendor }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      <h1 class="product__title">{{ product.title }}</h1>
      <p class="product__meta">
        {%- if product.model != blank %}Model {{ product.model }}{% endif -%}
        {%- if product.weight != blank %} · {{ product.weight }}{% endif -%}
      </p>
      <p class="product__price">{{ product.price | money }}</p>

      {%- comment -%}
        novalidate on purpose: chip groups post through a hidden input, which the browser never
        validates, so leaving native validation on would give selects one error style and chips
        another. theme.js validates every option group the same way instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <form novalidate
            data-product-form
            data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
            data-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
            data-base-price="{{ product.price }}"
            data-image="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 120 }}">

        {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
          {% render 'product-options', option: option %}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The variant map. Shopify's /cart/add.js takes a VARIANT id and rejects a product id, and
          until 2026-08-15 this form carried only `data-product-id` — so every add-to-cart on a real
          Shopify store would have failed, while the preview (which has no variants and posts to a
          local driver) passed. `product-card.liquid` had it right with
          `first_available_variant.id`; the product page, the one place option selection actually
          happens, was the one place it was missing.

          Emitted as JSON rather than as attributes because the option-value combination is the key:
          theme.js joins the selected values in option order and looks the id up. In the preview this
          array is empty, the lookup finds nothing, and the local driver's existing product-id path
          still works — so the two runtimes diverge here honestly instead of the shim hiding it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <script type="application/json" data-variant-map>
          [
            {%- for v in product.variants -%}
              {"id": {{ v.id | json }}, "available": {{ v.available | json }},
               "price": {{ v.price | json }}, "options": {{ v.options | json }}}
              {%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        </script>

        <fieldset class="decoration">
          <legend>Decoration &amp; tailoring</legend>
          <p class="hint" style="margin-top:0;">
            Name tapes, embroidery, and hemming are quoted on the order ticket. Tell us what you need and we confirm
            before anything is charged.
          </p>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Name tape / embroidery text <span class="hint">(optional)</span></span>
            <input type="text" name="properties[Name tape]" maxlength="40" autocomplete="off">
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Notes for the tailor <span class="hint">(optional)</span></span>
            <textarea name="properties[Tailor notes]" maxlength="400"></textarea>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <label class="field" style="max-width:140px;">
          <span>Quantity</span>
          <input type="number" name="quantity" value="1" min="1" step="1" inputmode="numeric">
        </label>

        <p class="error-text" data-form-error hidden></p>
        <button class="btn btn--accent btn--full" type="submit">Add to order</button>
        <p class="hint" style="margin-top:.75rem;">
          Questions on fit or agency pricing? Call {{ settings.contact_phone | default: '(814) 536-2390' }}.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
